From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 05:25:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rk3566-pinetab2: restore sd-uhs-sdr104 on the WiFi SDIO bus

The BES2600 enumerates on the SDIO bus but its firmware download dies part
way through, and the chip then stops answering entirely:

    mmc2: new high speed SDIO card at address 0001
    (NULL device *): wait dpd data ready failed:-110      (SDIO read timed out)
    (NULL device *): read dpd data failed.
    (NULL device *): bes2600_sdio_probe failed, func:1
    bes2600_wlan mmc2:0001:2: probe with driver bes2600_wlan failed with error -123

The LuneOS 6.6 device tree, where WiFi worked, has an &sdmmc1 node identical
to this one in every respect except that sd-uhs-sdr104 is present; megi's
tree has it commented out. That is the whole difference:

    6.6:   sd-uhs-sdr104;
    7.2:   //sd-uhs-sdr104;

Without it the host caps out in high-speed mode - hence "new high speed SDIO
card" and a 50 MHz bus clock in the log - while vqmmc-supply still holds the
I/O rail at 1.8V via vcca1v8_pmu. Enumeration and the small register reads
that follow are tolerant of that; the multi-hundred-kilobyte firmware
download is where it stops being tolerant, which is exactly where this fails.

Things already ruled out by experiment, recorded so they are not retried:

  - the driver driving the chip's power-enable low (powerup-gpios removed from
    the bes2600 node in 0005: the message goes away, the DPD failure does not)
  - the factory calibration data, including the select_efuse field we
    synthesise (renamed the file away: driver reports "factory cali data get
    failed" and the DPD stage fails identically)
  - mmc-pwrseq-bes being absent (pwrseq_bes.o is obj-y, always built)

TESTED 2026-09-09: DOES NOT HELP - do not re-apply without new evidence.

With this patch the host does offer UHS, but the card never completes the
1.8V handshake, so mmc_set_uhs_voltage() returns -EAGAIN and the core retries
ten times, power-cycling the chip on each round, before giving up:

    mmc2: Skipping voltage switch
    mmc2: new high speed SDIO card at address 0001

i.e. the bus ends in exactly the same high-speed 50 MHz mode as without the
patch, so 6.6 must have landed there too and bus mode is not the difference.
The DPD failure is unchanged. Net effect is ten extra power cycles at init,
so this is left out of SRC_URI.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration]
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -855,7 +855,7 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&sdmmc1_bus4
 		     &sdmmc1_cmd
 		     &sdmmc1_clk>;
-	//sd-uhs-sdr104;
+	sd-uhs-sdr104;
 	vqmmc-supply = <&vcca1v8_pmu>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
